<title>UK: World Bank sets 100 bln lire zero-coupon bond.</title>
<headline>World Bank sets 100 bln lire zero-coupon bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The World Bank has issued a 100 billion lire zero-coupon five-year bond, with redemption linked to the MIB 30 index, joint lead managers J.P. Morgan and San Paolo said.</p>
<p> BORROWER   WORLD BANK</p>
<p> AMT    100 BLN LIRE  COUPON     ZERO	MATURITY    28.AUG.02</p>
<p> TYPE	 **	  ISS PRICE  101.60    PAY DATE    =d.mmm.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.75	REOFFER    100 (RECOMMENDED)</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    LUX</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (M) ONE	 SALE LIMITS US.UK/IT</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  SUPRA     TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.15	SELL CONC  1.60	PRAECIPUUM  NONE</p>
<p> NOTES	**EQUITY LINKED VARIABLE REDEMPTION NOTE</p>
<p>		REDEMPTION IS BASED ON MIB 30 INDEX PERFORMANCE OVER</p>
<p>		THE 30 MONTHS BEFORE MATURITY. GUARANTEED MINIMUM</p>
<p>		REDEMPTION 4.50 PCT.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
